This product includes software developed by the HQ-SAM authors, extracted from the
Segment Anything in High Quality project (https://github.com/SysCV/sam-hq) and reduced
to its single-image inference path. HQ-SAM is built on Meta's Segment Anything
(https://github.com/facebookresearch/segment-anything); the files carried from it keep
Meta's copyright header. Both are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; see the
LICENSE file in this directory.

The published checkpoints are Apache-2.0 as well, stated on the model card of the
repository the authors serve them from (https://huggingface.co/lkeab/hq-sam). They contain
Meta's SAM weights (Apache-2.0) or, for the tiny variant, MobileSAM's TinyViT encoder
(Apache-2.0, https://github.com/ChaoningZhang/MobileSAM), with HQ-SAM's trained
parameters on top.

The tiny variant's image encoder, tiny_vit.py, is TinyViT, carried through MobileSAM and
HQ-SAM. Its header names its origin, and Microsoft's licence for it is reproduced here as
